    "content": "$1 - 2\\sqrt{3}$",
    "rationale": "This is minus the denominator; the product $-\\left(2\\sqrt{3} - 1\\right)^{2}$ still contains a surd."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "For a denominator $a\\sqrt{b} - c$, multiply by its conjugate $a\\sqrt{b} + c$; the product $a^{2}b - c^{2}$ is rational.",
